{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>הגוי גם צדיק תהרוג</b> [would you kill even a righteous nation?]: on behalf of himself, his household, and his kingdom. And likewise it is written, <b>ואל תשמע אל דברי חולם החלום המחליף מלה במלה</b> [and do not listen to the words of a dreaming dreamer who exchanges one word for another], in which <b>הגוי</b> means 'the man.' And regarding the word <b>לעם נכרי</b> (Exodus 21:8) I shall elaborate a little."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase from Deuteronomy 13:2–4 ('ואל תשמע...') appears here as a scriptural parallel for הגוי meaning 'the man'; the citation is implicit and the connection between the passages is left unexplained, consistent with Ibn Ezra's terseness."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:15.046609779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}